Subject: The generator export carries the digest of every function in a function's constant pool

What this does
  - `JSAotGenFunc` gets `cpool_fn`: one 16-byte digest per constant-pool entry, all zero when the entry is not a materialized
    register-compiled function. It is filled for every function with a pool, whether or not the pool has numbers, and freed with the rest.

Why we need it
  The generator can then follow a `make_closure` to the function it creates, to attribute methods to classes and resolve callees. A zero
  digest is an unresolved function, which the scan treats as an unknown callee.

Functions touched
  `js_aot_gen_collect`, `js_aot_gen_free`, `JSAotGenFunc`. Generator build only; nothing in a running engine reads it.

No.

